## 1. Purpose and Intended Use

This educational prototype compares several NLP approaches for assigning a dominant food-hazard category to short incident reports:

- Biological
- Allergen
- Physical
- Chemical

It is designed for exploring tradeoffs between speed, interpretability, zero-shot generalization, and learned language patterns. It is not a regulatory, clinical, or production food-safety system.

---

## 2. Installation

### Requirements

- Python 3.9 or later
- pip

### Setup

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/A-Kuo/Food-Hazard-Tiny-Model-Evaluation.git](https://github.com/A-Kuo/Food-Hazard-Tiny-Model-Evaluation.git)
cd Food-Hazard-Tiny-Model-Evaluation
pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m streamlit run app.py
```

Streamlit prints a local address, typically:

```text
http://localhost:8501
```

---

## 3. Optional GPT-2 Setup

The GPT-2 semantic-centroid baseline is optional because it requires downloading transformer weights.

1. Uncomment the following dependencies in `requirements.txt`:

```text
transformers>=4.38.0
torch>=2.0.0
```

2. Reinstall dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

3. Restart the dashboard:

```bash
python -m streamlit run app.py
```

The first run may download approximately 500 MB of model weights.

